.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-BUILD-AETHER-SESSION 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-build-aether-session
.Nd build and test the pinned offline Aether serial-shell candidate
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/build-aether-session.py
.Ar output
.Op Fl Fl tools Ar paths.json
.Op Fl Fl smoke Ar immediate|delayed
.Op Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Run from the source repository root with recorded macOS arm64 tools.
Output must be fresh under existing out/ without symlink or traversal components.
Locked inputs, complete archive membership and executable hashes are verified
before staging. The owner is rebuilt to exact qualified raw and ELF bytes;
sealed kernel/client/firmware binaries are reused. All six boot components are
read back. This command does not fetch, install or modify sibling repositories.
.Fl Fl tools
relocates identical executable bytes without changing hashes.
.Fl Fl smoke
runs three fragmented prompt-driven commands through exact output, identity,
terminal, cleanup and authorized-halt checks. Delayed input waits 35 seconds at
the first prompt and two seconds at later prompts.
.Sh OUTPUT
Plain ASCII progress/errors use stderr. One result JSON uses stdout.
Owned output retains result.json, phase logs, sources, notices and artifact hashes.
Smoke retains serial.log, qemu.stderr and smoke.json. Failures retain their output.
The result console_argv supports a separate manual serial development boot after
artifact/tool freshness checks; it is not an acceptance oracle.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 operational failure; 2 blocked precondition; 64 invalid usage;
130 keyboard interruption. Help and version exit 0 on stdout.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/build-aether-session.py out/my-session --smoke immediate
python3 scripts/build-aether-session.py out/idle-session --smoke delayed
.Ed
.Sh LIMITATIONS
This is a developer ABI24/AENMX009 candidate, not installed or released init.
No automatic restart, login, general TTY/job control or persistence is provided.
Tool bounds are 180 seconds/4 MiB; guest bounds are 90 seconds, 1 MiB UART and
4 MiB stderr. Live owned groups are stopped and children reaped. Fatal/repeated
signals and detached tools are outside this guarantee. Complete dependency closure,
filesystem deadlines and host sandboxing are not claimed. Build-only success is
not native acceptance. Remaining negative/cleanup qualification and independent
assembled review are separate.
.Sh SEE ALSO
docs/AETHER-SESSION.md, docs/aether-session.lock.json,
docs/SERIAL-BOOT-COMPOSITION.md
